title: Choosing Our Enemies
new-page: true
view-if: year <= 1930 and enemies_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; enemies_timer = 18
max-visits: 3
is-card: true
card-image: img/poster_1.png
tags: party_affairs

= Choosing our enemies

In our media and campaign materials, who should we consider as our main opponents?

[? if enemies != 0 : Previously, we had considered the [+ enemies +] as our prior enemies. Is a change of direction necessary? ?]

- @anti_dem: The anti-democratic parties of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-[? if dnvp_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span>?][? if dnvp_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #003755;">right</span>?] and <span style="color: #700000;">left</span> - the <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span>, <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span>, and [? if dnvp_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>?][? if dnvp_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #003755;">**DNF**</span>?].
- @far_right: The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-[? if dnvp_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span>?][? if dnvp_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #003755;">right</span>?] - the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span> and [? if dnvp_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>?][? if dnvp_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #003755;">**DNF**</span>?].
- @nsdap: The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span> alone.
- @kpd: The <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span>.
- @left: The Leftist parties of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span> and <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span>.
- @easy_discard

@anti_dem
on-arrival: enemies = "anti-democratic parties"; left_strength += 5; labor_strength += 5; left_dissent -= 5; workers_kpd -= 1.5; workers_nsdap -= 2; workers_dnvp -= 1 if dnvp_ideology == "Radical"; workers_dnf -= 1; unemployed_kpd -= 2; unemployed_nsdap -= 2; kpd_relation -= 10; spd_relation += 5; dnvp_relation -= 5

Attacking the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-[? if dnvp_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span>?][? if dnvp_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #003755;">right</span>?] and <span style="color: #700000;">left</span> is popular among all but the left wing of our party, who would prefer to be fighting the bourgeois parties. This might also hamper our ability to reconcile with the <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span> in the future.

@far_right
on-arrival: enemies = "far right"; left_strength += 5; left_dissent -= 5; workers_nsdap -= 3; unemployed_nsdap -= 3; workers_dnvp -= 2 if dnvp_ideology == "Radical"; workers_dnf -= 2 spd_relation += 5; dnvp_relation -=5

Attacking the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> is popular among the <span style="color: #FF7F00;">Christian Left</span>, while the <span style="color: #000000;">Center</span> to be just as dangerous, and the right all but completely opposes this move. Our bourgeois coalition partners are also skeptical of our lack of commitment to anti-communism, However,the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span> is very supportive.


@nsdap
on-arrival: enemies = "NSDAP"; left_strength += 5; nazi_urgency += 1; workers_nsdap -= 4; unemployed_nsdap -= 4;  spd_relation += 5; workers_nsdap += 8 if nsdap_votes < 8; unemployed_nsdap += 8 if nsdap_votes < 8

[? if nazi_urgency == 0 or nsdap_votes < 10: The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span> is a tiny party right now, with more bark than bite. Many in our party are questioning our choices. [? if nsdap_votes < 8: Worst still, giving them too much attention might only end up helping them. ?] ?][? if nazi_urgency > 0 and nsdap_votes >= 10 : The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazis</span> are the most urgent problem for us to deal with. ?]

@kpd
on-arrival: enemies = "KPD"; reformist_strength += 5; left_dissent += 2; reformist_dissent -= 5; kpd_relation -= 15; dvp_relation += 5; ddp_relation += 3; lvp_relation += 5; workers_kpd -= 3; unemployed_kpd -= 4; dvp_left += 1; ddp_left += 0.5; ddp_cohesion += 0.5; lvp_left += 1

Attacking the <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span> is supported by all but the most left-wing members, and wins us approval among the bourgeois parties. However, If we are to build relations with the <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span> this may not be the best choice.

@left
on-arrival: enemies = "bourgeois parties"; reformist_strength += 8; reformist_dissent -= 5; dvp_relation += 5; lvp_relation += 5; dnvp_relation += 10; kpd_relation -= 10; workers_spd -= 4; spd_relation -= 10; workers_kpd += 5; coalition_dissent += 1 

Attacking the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span> and <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span> pleases our right wing and wins us some favor among the bourgeois parties and the DNVP. The <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span> and <span style="color: #FF7F00;">Christian Left</span> are displeased.

 
